# Applies to builds that use backend/Dockerfile.
#
# Two things to know, both of which this file previously got wrong:
#
# 1. Patterns are relative to the BUILD CONTEXT root, which docker-compose sets
#    to the repo root — not to backend/. A bare `.env` therefore only ever
#    matched a root-level .env, while `COPY backend/ .` happily copied
#    backend/.env, baking DATABASE_URL and PUBLICKEY into the image.
# 2. There are no trailing comments. `.env*  # ignore env files` is one literal
#    pattern including the '#' and everything after it, so it matches nothing.
#
# Secrets reach the container through the environment (see docker-compose), never
# by being copied in.

**/node_modules/
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
.git/
